# ORDERING -- MEASURED, and now really declared in scripts/check-patch-order.py
# ============================================================================
# An earlier version of this header asserted "all of these are declared in
# scripts/check-patch-order.py". They were NOT: the checker exited 1 on three
# unclassified pairs, and this patch was the only thing keeping that gate red.
# LW-M4-04's second pass measured each pair and added the rows. The method is
# the one LW-M4-05 used: replay each shared file on its own through the whole
# android apply sequence in list order and then with the pair swapped, and
# compare sha256 plus patch's exit status and .rej files.
#
# TWO of the pairs turned out to be HARD CONSTRAINTS, not offsets:
#
#   no-adjust  ->  no-crashreporter      MANDATORY (2 of its 3 shared files)
#     * fenix app/build.gradle: this patch's hunk 2 (@@ -391,7 +391,6 @@,
#       deleting SENTRY_TOKEN from android.buildTypes.debug) has trailing
#       context that no longer contains the ADJUST_TOKEN line directly below
#       it -- the line no-adjust's @@ -406,7 +399,6 @@ deletes. Swap the pair
#       and the hunk REJECTS (patch exits 1, one .rej).
#     * Analytics.kt: this patch's hunk 1 (@@ -13,21 +13,9 @@) spans the import
#       block from runtimetagproviders.BuildRuntimeTagProvider to
#       components.metrics.MetricController, a range that in the pristine file
#       still holds the AdjustMetricsService and InstallReferrerMetricsService
#       imports. It REJECTS too, and fuzz does not rescue it.
#     * Components.kt is order-free (byte-identical either way).
#
#   no-gms     ->  no-crashreporter      MANDATORY (1 of its 3 shared files)
#     * mobile/android/focus-android/app/build.gradle: this patch's hunk 2
#       (@@ -315,7 +318,8 @@, deleting `implementation libs.sentry`) has
#       leading context google.material / kotlinx.coroutines / mozilla.glean,
#       and in the pristine file the two lines no-gms deletes --
#       libs.play.review and libs.play.review.ktx -- sit between glean and
#       sentry. Swap the pair and that hunk REJECTS.
#     * fenix app/build.gradle and Components.kt are order-free, byte-identical
#       either way -- worth stating, because the checker's overlap HINT calls
#       fenix app/build.gradle "overlap or abut" for this pair and is wrong.
#
# ONE pair is genuinely order-free, and the honest caveat comes with it:
#
#   no-glean  <->  no-crashreporter      ORDER-FREE, but leans on fuzz
#     Both shared files (fenix app/build.gradle, Analytics.kt) come out
#     byte-identical either way with patch exiting 0 and no .rej. With
#     no-crashreporter first, its import hunk lands "with fuzz 1" (no-glean's
#     Glean*MetricsService imports are still inside its context) and no-glean's
#     own hunk then also lands with fuzz 1. In LIST order both apply at fuzz 0.
#     This is the only row here that depends on fuzz.
#
# The GeckoProvider.kt pairs (about-config LW-M4-09, isolated-process LW-M5-02)
# were already classified order-free: three disjoint regions of one file.
#
# So the position in assets/patches/android.txt is fixed on both sides: AFTER
# no-adjust, no-glean and no-gms, and BEFORE patches/android/build-fixes.patch,
# which is the collection point for build breakage and is documented as last.
