# zero on the right a measurement rather than an absence of evidence.
#
# WHAT A USER IS LEFT WITH -- measured, not inferred. On the patched build,
# after one uncaught exception:
#   * the on-device Room DB `crashes` has 1 row: crashType UNCAUGHT, a uuid,
#     the full stack trace, breadcrumbs and runtime tags. The `reports` table
#     has 0 rows -- nothing was submitted anywhere.
#   * typing "about:crashes" into the Fenix toolbar opens the crash list
#     (mozac_lib_crash_list / _id / _title / _footer) showing the uuid, the
#     exception line, and a footer reading "<when> - Share".
#     NOTE FOR WHOEVER AUTOMATES THIS: "Share" is a ClickableSpan at the RIGHT
#     END of mozac_lib_crash_footer, not a button with its own id -- tapping the
#     view's centre lands on the timestamp and does nothing. Tapped at the right
#     edge (footer bounds [11,181]-[446,234], tap at 416,207) it DOES open
